after:
{"category": "Personality change", "description": "I find that the plaintiff suffered a severe head injury with mild adjustment disorder as a result of the Accident. he was found to have had a concussion, hemorrhage in the brain, fractured temporal bones, and showed signs of vomiting and amnesia. CT scan of the plaintiff revealed the following:

i. Bilateral subarachnoid hemorrhage;

ii. Subdural hemorrhage overlying right cerebrum and along bilateral tentorium;

iii. Hyperdense contusions in left frontal and right temporal lobes; and

iv. Extraaxial hematoma in left frontal region, could be subdural or epidural hematoma. The plaintiff was diagnosed to have suffered from adjustment disorder with mixed anxiety and depressive reaction.", "caused_by_injury_id": "inj_001"}
